       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin in adults. At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the labeled maximum.\n- **1,700 mg per day**, divided as 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily**, or another dose that fits the patient's glycemic needs and tolerance.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really intend a dose above the labeled maximum, it will need to go through pharmacy or the prescriber outside this tool. I can't enter it on the basis of a stated approval."
      }
